# Chittu demo box — copy to .env beside compose.yaml, fill in, chmod 600.
# The filled-in .env lives on the box only. Never commit it.

# REQUIRED. Generate once:  openssl rand -base64 32
#
# The dev key provider encrypts parent email, child first name, message bodies
# and memory facts under this key. It must stay the same for the life of the
# demo data: lose or rotate it and every stored row becomes unreadable — which
# is the crypto-shred property working as designed, just pointed at yourself.
# (Also an acceptable outcome for a demo: wipe the volume and re-onboard.)
CHITTU_DEV_MASTER_KEY=

# Optional. Absent => the stub router (the API announces this on its first log
# line): consent, chat, CPA maths, the crisis turn + lock + parent unlock, L1
# guards, memory book, dashboard and seal verify all demo fully — those paths
# make zero model calls by design. With a key, the L2 classifier and L5 sandbox
# run against Anthropic. Use a low-limit key; it lives on a demo box.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional — the automated ID check (G1 consent rail, Didit).
#
# Absent => the method is not offered to a parent and the API announces that on
# boot. Present => real parents photograph real government IDs, so this is a
# deliberate act: G1 is recorded as blocked on a DPO/DPIA decision about a
# processor handling parents' biometrics.
#
# The workflow id names a configuration and authorises nothing, so it is not a
# secret. The API key is. DIDIT_ENVIRONMENT is allowlisted ('live'/'sandbox') —
# an unrecognised value refuses at boot rather than being guessed.
#
# DIDIT_CALLBACK_URL must be the PUBLIC origin. A localhost value copied from a
# developer's .env.local sends every parent back to their own machine, and the
# failure is silent: the vendor reports success and the flow simply never
# completes.
#DIDIT_API_KEY=
#DIDIT_WORKFLOW_ID=c53d125d-d09e-47d0-a16a-5c0ade2b9c7e
#DIDIT_ENVIRONMENT=live
#DIDIT_CALLBACK_URL=https://chittu.tulifo.ai/?idcheck=return

# Optional overrides.
#POSTGRES_PASSWORD=chittu
#LOG_LEVEL=info
